# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 4 — G6: the trailing guard WITHOUT the per-iteration one.
#
# ⛔ ONE-DIFFERENCE CONTROL against G0, and the file that stops slice 5 from shipping the simpler
# thing. `g3_trailing_guard.ebnf` carries BOTH guards; the obvious question is whether the trailing
# one subsumes the loop one, since it constrains the rule's whole result rather than each step.
#
#   G0:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )*
#   G6:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )* &( tick lparen lit rparen )
#   G2:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )*
#   G3:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )* &( tick lparen lit rparen )
#
# REQUIRED VERDICTS: **REJECT** on e1–e4 and e6, **ACCEPT** on e5 — the exact complement of G2.
#
# ⭐⭐ WHAT IT PINS: THE TWO GUARD POSITIONS CLOSE DISJOINT STARVATIONS, and neither is redundant.
#   * The per-iteration guard stops the LOOP at the right count. The trailing guard cannot: by the
#     time it runs, the possessive `*` has already committed to the maximum count and there is no
#     give-back to a shorter one — so on `k = n'(n);` the loop has eaten the holder's residual and
#     the trailing guard can only turn a starved parse into a failed one.
#   * The trailing guard refuses an over-long SEED. The per-iteration guard cannot: on
#     `k = t'(n);` the loop takes ZERO iterations and never runs, while `prim_base`'s sheared clone
#     has already matched the whole cast.
#
# ⇒ the transformation owes BOTH, on the same clone. That is one clone chain carrying two lookaheads,
# not two clone chains — the cost statement `.17` acceptance (a) has to price.
@entry: true
scratch := kw_k eq outer_cast semi
outer_cast := ct tick lparen lit rparen
ct := kw | prim
prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )* &( tick lparen lit rparen )
prim_base := lit | cast_seed
cast_seed := kw tick lparen lit rparen
prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen

lit := trivia /n/
kw := trivia /t/
kw_k := trivia /k/
eq := trivia "="
semi := trivia ";"
tick := trivia "'"
lparen := trivia "("
rparen := trivia ")"

@branch_policy: priority_first
trivia := (line_comment | block_comment)*
line_comment := /\/\/[^\n]*(\n|$)/
block_comment := /\/\*([^*]|\*+[^*\/])*\*+\//
